# Sandbox structure

Single Flutter app (`sandbox`) managed with Melos (`useRootAsPackage: true`). Features are folders under `lib/`, not separate packages.

```
lib/
  main.dart, app.dart, home_page.dart   # shell, tabs, GoRouter
  di/di.dart                            # configureDependencies()
  routing/routes.dart                   # TypedGoRoute + routes.g.dart
  shared/di/di.dart                     # GetIt instance `get`
  shared/view/widgets/                  # widgets used by more than one feature
  <feature>/
    data/datasource/                    # Chopper APIs, local storage
    data/models/                        # DTOs (*_dto.dart, *.g.dart)
    data/repo/
    domain/models/
    domain/usecases/                    # *UC
    view/bloc/                          # bloc + freezed event/state parts
    view/model/
    view/page/                          # *_page.dart, *_content.dart
    view/widgets/
test/                                   # mirrors lib/ (test/news/view/…)
```

Existing features: `news`, `favorites`, `traffic_light`.

## Boundaries

- A feature may use `shared` and another feature's domain use cases (see `LoadNewsUC` and favorites). Keep widgets and blocs inside the owning feature.
- HTTP and persistence stay in `data/`. Pages talk to blocs.
- New experimental modules use the same `<feature>/` layout. Skip layers the module does not need (`traffic_light` has no remote API).

## Commands

Use FVM. Codegen: `fvm dart run melos run build_runner --no-select`. Format touched files with `fvm dart format --line-length=100`.
